/*
:name: comb_output_overflow_runtime
:type: error
:tolg: 1
:error: `o` \(range \[[01], 16\]\) (does|may) not fit its declared range \[0, 15\]
:help: (apply a wrap/saturate policy|`wrap`/`sat`)
*/
// A comb OUTPUT is a declared type like any other variable: `o:U4` holds
// [0, 15], and `o = a + 1` with a:U4 can produce 16. An unannotated narrowing
// assignment is a compile error (docs 04b "wrap and sat modifier": "Every
// narrowing assignment must annotate locally ... at every overflow-risking
// line"; docs 07 "The current should never exceed the constrained or a compile
// error is generated"), so the fix is `wrap o = a + 1` or `sat o = a + 1`.
// errors/comb_output_overflow_provable.prp is the case where every value
// overflows; this one only MAY overflow (x = 15), which is what the docs rule
// makes an error. Existing fixtures that rely on a silent may-overflow wrap
// (e.g. equiv/reserved_word_signal.prp `packed = a + 1`) need a `wrap` prefix
// when this rule lands.
//
// Today it compiles silently and the declared width is never applied to the
// inlined comb: x = 15 returns 16 through an `o:U4` output, while the
// standalone Verilog `module inc` (and the same body written as a `mod`) wraps
// to 0.
comb inc(a:U4) -> (o:U4) {
  o = a + 1   // locate_error_here
}

pub mod comb_output_overflow_runtime(x:U4) -> (y:U8@[0]) {
  y = inc(a=x)
}
